{
  "semantics": {
    "attributes": {
      "final": {},
      "header": {}
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "It is easy to create AOP proxies programmatically with Spring. This lets you use Spring AOP without dependency on Spring IoC."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The interfaces implemented by the target object are automatically proxied. The following listing shows creation of a proxy for a target object, with one interceptor and one advisor:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "dlist",
            "id": null,
            "items": [
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "context": "listing",
                      "id": null,
                      "inlines": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "ProxyFactory factory = new ProxyFactory(myBusinessInterfaceImpl);\nfactory.addAdvice(myMethodInterceptor);\nfactory.addAdvisor(myAdvisor);\nMyBusinessInterface tb = (MyBusinessInterface) factory.getProxy();"
                        }
                      ],
                      "language": "java",
                      "roles": [],
                      "title": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "checkbox": null,
                  "inlines": []
                },
                "terms": [
                  [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "Java"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              },
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "context": "listing",
                      "id": null,
                      "inlines": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "val factory = ProxyFactory(myBusinessInterfaceImpl)\nfactory.addAdvice(myMethodInterceptor)\nfactory.addAdvisor(myAdvisor)\nval tb = factory.proxy as MyBusinessInterface"
                        }
                      ],
                      "language": "kotlin",
                      "roles": [],
                      "title": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "checkbox": null,
                  "inlines": []
                },
                "terms": [
                  [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "Kotlin"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "example",
        "id": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The first step is to construct an object of type "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "org.springframework.aop.framework.ProxyFactory"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". You can create this with a target object, as in the preceding example, or specify the interfaces to be proxied in an alternate constructor."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "You can add advice (with interceptors as a specialized kind of advice), advisors, or both and manipulate them for the life of the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ProxyFactory"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". If you add an "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "IntroductionInterceptionAroundAdvisor"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", you can cause the proxy to implement additional interfaces."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "There are also convenience methods on "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ProxyFactory"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " (inherited from "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "AdvisedSupport"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ") that let you add other advice types, such as before and throws advice. "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "AdvisedSupport"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " is the superclass of both "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ProxyFactory"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ProxyFactoryBean"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "admonition",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Integrating AOP proxy creation with the IoC framework is best practice in most applications. We recommend that you externalize configuration from Java code with AOP, as you should in general."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null,
        "type": "tip"
      }
    ],
    "outline": null,
    "title": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "value": "Creating AOP Proxies Programmatically with the "
      },
      {
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "ProxyFactory"
          }
        ],
        "kind": "monospace",
        "roles": []
      }
    ]
  }
}
